D("particle",{etymology:E("From Latin particula ‘little bit, small part’, diminutive of pars ‘part’; the word later acquired scientific and grammatical senses.",null,"pars","-icle","Etymonline, particle (https://www.etymonline.com/word/particle)."),contexts:[C("particle.s1","通用","A dust particle drifted through the sunbeam and settled on the dark windowsill.","一粒灰塵在陽光中飄動，最後落在深色窗台上。","A particle is an extremely small piece of a substance.","Dust particle is the subject; and links its movement and result.","The tiny piece of dust is visible only in the beam of light."),C("particle.s2","物理","The detector records each particle that passes through the chamber during the experiment.","探測器會記錄實驗中每個穿過腔室的粒子。","In physics, a particle is a very small unit of matter such as an electron.","Each particle is the object of records; that introduces the relative clause.","The experiment counts subatomic units as they cross the chamber."),C("particle.s3","語言","In “look it up,” the word up is a particle that combines with the verb to form a phrasal verb.","在 look it up 這個短語中，up 是與動詞結合構成短語動詞的小品詞。","A grammatical particle is a short, usually uninflected word with a function in a phrase or construction.","The quoted example illustrates the term; that clause explains its grammatical role.","Up combines with look rather than acting as a freely inflected verb.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","In the phrasal verb “turn down,” down is a particle because it changes freely into downed to show tense.","In the phrasal verb “turn down,” down is a particle because it stays unchanged while the verb carries tense.","The particle itself does not inflect for tense; the verb changes form.")],quiz:[Q("particle.q1","particle.s1","meaning","A particle of dust is ___.",["a very small piece of matter","a complete weather system","a large piece of furniture"],"a very small piece of matter","The ordinary sense is a tiny piece of something.","meaning"),Q("particle.q2","particle.s2","context","Which item is a particle in physics?",["An electron studied by a detector","A whole laboratory building","A textbook’s chapter title"],"An electron studied by a detector","An electron is a subatomic particle.","context"),Q("particle.q3","particle.s3","meaning","In “give up,” the word up is a grammatical ___.",["particle","paragraph","predicate noun"],"particle","Up combines with the verb to form a phrasal verb.","meaning"),Q("particle.q4","particle.s3","grammar","Choose the particle in “They looked the address up.”",["up","they","address"],"up","Up joins with looked to form the phrasal verb looked up.","grammar")]});
D("particular",{etymology:E("From Old French particuler and Late Latin particularis ‘of a part’, from Latin particula ‘small part’; the adjective developed senses for a specific item, something special, or exacting attention.",null,"particula","-ar","Etymonline, particular (https://www.etymonline.com/word/particular)."),contexts:[C("particular.s1","通用","The clerk needs a particular receipt from Tuesday, not the folder of invoices from the whole month.","職員需要星期二的那張特定收據，而不是整個月的發票資料夾。","Particular means one specific person or thing rather than others.","Attributive adjective before receipt; not contrasts the one item with a larger set.","Tuesday’s receipt is singled out from all the other records."),C("particular.s2","通用","The coastal path offers a particular kind of quiet at dawn, before the fishing boats return.","黎明時、漁船返航之前，海岸步道有一種格外的寧靜。","Particular can mean special or greater than usual.","A particular kind of quiet describes a distinctive quality; before gives the time.","The quiet is presented as distinctive, not ordinary."),C("particular.s3","通用","My aunt is particular about the way her tea is brewed and asks for the water just below boiling.","我姑媽對泡茶方式很講究，總要求水溫略低於沸點。","Particular can mean difficult to please because someone wants things done in an exact way.","Particular about is followed by the subject of exacting preference.","She specifies a precise temperature rather than accepting any preparation."),C("particular.s4","通用","The investigator asked for the particulars of the delivery, including its date, route, and recipient.","調查員要求提供送貨的細節，包括日期、路線和收件人。","A particular is one fact or detail; particulars commonly means details.","The particulars of introduces the facts requested; including lists examples.","The investigator needs specific details about the delivery.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The clerk requested a particular receipt but accepted any document from any month without checking which one it was.","The clerk requested a particular receipt and checked that it was the one issued on Tuesday.","Particular identifies a specific item; accepting any document ignores the required specificity.")],quiz:[Q("particular.q1","particular.s1","context","Which request asks for one particular file?",["Bring the blue folder labeled “April audit.”","Bring any folder from any year.","Bring nothing from the cabinet."],"Bring the blue folder labeled “April audit.”","The label singles out one specific file.","context"),Q("particular.q2","particular.s2","meaning","A particular pleasure is ___.",["a special or distinctive pleasure","a pleasure that never occurs","a rule against enjoyment"],"a special or distinctive pleasure","Particular can mean special or greater than usual.","meaning"),Q("particular.q3","particular.s3","meaning","Someone particular about food may ___.",["insist on specific preparation details","eat anything without preference","forget that food exists"],"insist on specific preparation details","This sense is exacting about how something should be done.","meaning"),Q("particular.q4","particular.s4","word-choice","The form asks for the ____ of the incident, such as its time and place.",["particulars","particulate","participator"],"particulars","Particulars means the specific facts or details.","word-choice")]});
