D("particularly",{etymology:E("Formed from particular + -ly; it is used to single out something as especially notable or to a greater degree than other things.",null,"particular","-ly","Etymonline, particularly (https://www.etymonline.com/word/particularly)."),contexts:[C("particularly.s1","语法","The trail is particularly slippery near the waterfall, where mist settles on the stone steps.","瀑布附近的步道特別濕滑，因為霧氣會落在石階上。","Particularly means more than usually or more than other things.","Adverb modifies slippery; where explains the local condition.","The waterfall area is more slippery than the rest of the trail.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The road was particularly dry after the storm because standing water covered every lane.","The road was particularly wet after the storm because standing water covered every lane.","Water covering every lane describes wetness, the opposite of dry.")],quiz:[Q("particularly.q1","particularly.s1","meaning","If one room is particularly warm, it is ___.",["warmer than usual or the others","the coldest room in the house","not warmer in any way"],"warmer than usual or the others","Particularly marks a notably greater degree.","meaning"),Q("particularly.q2","particularly.s1","context","Which detail is particularly important?",["A cracked beam supporting the roof","A decorative label on an empty box","A color choice unrelated to the repair"],"A cracked beam supporting the roof","The beam matters more than incidental details because it supports the roof.","context"),Q("particularly.q3","particularly.s1","grammar","Choose the adverb: “The test was ____ difficult for beginners.”",["particularly","particular","particularity"],"particularly","The adverb modifies the adjective difficult.","grammar"),Q("particularly.q4","particularly.s1","word-choice","She was ____ pleased with the careful translation.",["particularly","particle","partake"],"particularly","The sentence means she was especially pleased.","word-choice")]});
